# Simple models

- Models are a list of fields plus `__str__`. That is enough.
- Do not add service methods, status machines, or extra managers on models.
- Tiny helpers like `is_admin` on User are OK (one line).
- No `UniqueConstraint` helpers if `unique_together` is clearer for this intern project — keep whatever already exists; do not add more Meta options.

```python
# GOOD
class Course(models.Model):
    title = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    description = models.TextField()
    pdf = models.FileField(upload_to="courses/pdfs/")

    def __str__(self):
        return self.title
```
